}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\operatorname{Or}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\operatorname{Imp}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\operatorname{Eqv}^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}:\n(F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})^2\\to F^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93}.\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}classical\\text{-}propositional\\text{-}calculus}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}classical\\text{-}propositional\\text{-}calculus}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}(\\mathcal P^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\n\\mathsf L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93},\\mathcal L^{\\mathsf{CPL}}_{93})\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom fixes the standard implication-negation Hilbert calculus: three classical axiom schemes and the single modus-ponens rule. Connectives and variables use disjoint explicit tags. Its two-element algebra supplies an independently defined semantics; completeness and Craig interpolation remain separate theorems rather than clauses of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}\">\\(\\mathrm{CPLPres}_{93}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-similarity-type","status":"resolved","id":"ee84ed8b0fae5bc3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-similarity-type]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-algebra","status":"resolved","id":"6730349967b8ffce","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[9